# Task Specification: Class Relationship Detection and Visualization

## Objective

Act as a Senior C# Developer. Your task is to extend our static analysis tool to detect class relationships. 
Enhance the existing static analysis engine to detect and export structural relationships between classes. The system must distinguish between standard class inheritance, abstract class inheritance, and interface implementation.

1. Core Logic: Relationship Extraction
The analysis engine (likely using Roslyn / Microsoft.CodeAnalysis) must be updated to inspect BaseList syntax or ITypeSymbol properties.

Relationship Categories:

Inheritance: When a class derives from another non-abstract class.

Abstract Inheritance: When a class derives from a class marked with the abstract modifier.

Implementation: When a class or interface implements one or multiple interfaces.

Metadata to Capture:

Source Entity (the child/implementer).

Target Entity (the parent/interface).

Relationship Type (Inheritance vs. Implementation).


2. Exporter Updates
Mermaid Exporter
Update the Mermaid generation logic to use standard Class Diagram syntax:

Inheritance (Class/Abstract): Parent <|-- Child

Implementation (Interface): Interface <|.. Class

Note: If the Parent is an abstract class, ensure the label or style indicates it (e.g., class Parent <<Abstract>>).

HTML/SVG Exporter

Update the SVG rendering engine to visually differentiate the connectors:

Solid Line + Hollow Arrowhead: Class/Abstract Inheritance.

Dashed Line + Hollow Arrowhead: Interface Implementation.

Color Coding (Optional): Use a specific CSS class for abstract connections (e.g., .relation-abstract) to allow distinct styling.

